WEBVTT

00:46.130 --> 00:54.900
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:54.940 --> 01:03.940
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

01:03.980 --> 01:10.710
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:13.320 --> 01:19.390
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:21.560 --> 01:30.130
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:30.170 --> 01:36.770
And I'm faced with another day

01:37.980 --> 01:43.710
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:43.750 --> 01:48.050
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:48.090 --> 01:52.530
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:52.560 --> 01:56.960
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:57.000 --> 02:01.490
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:01.540 --> 02:09.380
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:21.060 --> 02:23.310
These are collectively called
the Scroll of the "Nine Faces of Death."

02:24.140 --> 02:26.190
This is the "swelling" phase...

02:26.190 --> 02:28.020
This is called the "blood-stained" phase...

02:28.270 --> 02:30.780
The next is called the "rotting" phase...

02:30.900 --> 02:33.820
Maggots have burst from the inflamed and rotten flesh...

02:34.700 --> 02:37.320
Oh? What's wrong, Momosuke-han?

02:34.700 --> 02:38.320
[Note: -han is the same title suffix as -san, but
it is used by people from the Kyoto area]

02:38.330 --> 02:41.040
No, I'm just uncomfortable with this kind of thing.

02:41.040 --> 02:44.160
For a person collecting strange
stories, you have a weak stomach.

02:44.580 --> 02:47.540
Fushimiya-dono, please get to the point.

02:47.790 --> 02:51.670
This is the assistant to Kyoto's municipal magistrate,

02:51.670 --> 02:53.460
Sajuurou Ogata-sama.

02:53.470 --> 02:56.340
He is a colleague of Genba Sasayama-sama, over there.

02:57.180 --> 02:59.680
This meeting was arranged

02:59.680 --> 03:03.930
in regards to the strange events on Katabira
Street that have had the city in an uproar lately.

03:04.310 --> 03:06.060
I've heard the rumors.

03:06.060 --> 03:08.520
The bodies of four women have appeared on the street--

03:07.770 --> 03:08.810
That is correct.

03:08.810 --> 03:12.400
We wish to borrow your
wisdom to help us solve this problem.

03:12.400 --> 03:14.320
Wait, there's no way
somebody like me could help with that--

03:14.990 --> 03:18.320
That would be correct if it were a humans doing,

03:18.320 --> 03:20.030
but what if it were a monster's?

03:20.780 --> 03:21.660
What did you say?

03:22.160 --> 03:24.040
This is the origin of Katabira Street:

03:24.040 --> 03:28.460
It is said that when a certain
emperor's queen passed away,

03:28.460 --> 03:31.340
her body was left exposed to the elements,

03:31.340 --> 03:37.180
[Note: The shroud was a katabira, a lightweight kimono
undergarment inscribed with Buddhist mantras.]

03:31.340 --> 03:34.260
and her shroud fell off onto the street.

03:34.260 --> 03:37.180
The body of the empress was thrown into the street?

03:37.430 --> 03:40.800
Yes, and it was apparently in accordance with her will.

03:42.560 --> 03:44.720
No matter how beautiful something is,

03:44.730 --> 03:46.430
it will eventually decay.

03:47.060 --> 03:50.650
The empress, a devout Buddhist,
who knew the transience of all things,

03:50.650 --> 03:53.190
showed the transience of the world with her own body

03:55.740 --> 03:59.700
in order to terminate the
obsession the emperor had with her.

04:00.660 --> 04:02.450
Because of such tales,

04:02.450 --> 04:06.410
it has also been said that a
strange ghostly aura enveloped that street.

04:06.410 --> 04:07.960
That's when the incidents began to occur.

04:08.500 --> 04:10.120
There have been seven bodies.

04:10.250 --> 04:12.880
Some bodies have been stolen after death,

04:12.880 --> 04:16.420
some people have been kidnapped and killed, and then...

04:17.260 --> 04:20.760
After the bodies rotted,
they were discarded into the street.

04:20.760 --> 04:24.350
Furthermore, all of them were
beauties of some renown in the city.

04:24.350 --> 04:25.930
According to the rumors among the townsfolk,

04:25.930 --> 04:29.190
it is the doing of a female ghost who appears in the street.

04:29.270 --> 04:32.730
With a ghost as our opponent, the magistrate is helpless.

04:33.320 --> 04:35.730
That's where you come in:

04:35.730 --> 04:38.190
we were wondering if you had any
knowledge that could give us a clue...

04:38.780 --> 04:40.490
Even if you ask me...

04:40.490 --> 04:41.990
Please, anything?

04:41.990 --> 04:43.620
Er, but...

04:43.620 --> 04:54.920
[Note: Shimabara was a famous red light district in Kyoto.]

04:43.620 --> 04:49.330
Actually, one of the most
beautiful geisha in Shimabara, Kohagi,

04:49.330 --> 04:54.920
disappeared six months ago and hasn't been seen since.

04:57.670 --> 04:59.720
The geishas are here! Enjoy yourself.

05:00.760 --> 05:02.590
We will talk of this again later.

05:04.680 --> 05:06.430
Come, come in.

05:07.980 --> 05:10.520
Come in everyone. They've been waiting for this.

05:08.980 --> 05:11.810
Hey. Sasayama, come here, too.

05:11.560 --> 05:13.310
Hello everyone.

05:19.190 --> 05:22.110
Have a glass, you handsome man.

05:22.110 --> 05:24.410
Erm, well...

05:27.370 --> 05:28.290
Pervert.

05:29.120 --> 05:31.330
You were thinking of
something perverted again, weren't you?

05:32.000 --> 05:33.830
M-Me?

05:34.080 --> 05:35.460
I was not!

05:37.420 --> 05:40.720
So sensei, you are going to see this Fushimiya-san then?

05:40.720 --> 05:41.630
Yes,

05:41.800 --> 05:44.300
he's an acquaintance of my publisher, Tsutaya-san.

05:44.300 --> 05:47.140
He apparently likes strange
stories and asked me to visit him...

05:48.560 --> 05:51.430
Perhaps our relations have reached an end.

05:51.730 --> 05:52.480
Huh?

05:52.690 --> 06:01.490
[Note: A Komatakuguri deceives others with words as a profession.]

05:52.690 --> 05:55.650
Komatakuguri, you can't possibly mean...

05:56.440 --> 06:01.490
In other words, you live in a
different world from ours, sensei.

06:11.370 --> 06:12.750
Here, have a drink...

06:12.120 --> 06:14.210
Oops!

06:14.300 --> 06:16.130
You sure got me there!

06:14.360 --> 06:16.130
Have another.

06:25.550 --> 06:26.510
Sato...

06:31.980 --> 06:34.230
Sato, open your eyes! Sato!

06:51.200 --> 06:52.000
Sato!

07:00.910 --> 07:03.280
That was how it began.

07:03.280 --> 07:07.080
Then the first victim was Sasayama-sama's wife?

07:07.080 --> 07:12.250
Sasayama became quite depressed after his wife's death.

07:12.630 --> 07:16.250
Sometimes I invite him over for
entertainment like this lighten his spirits, but...

07:17.630 --> 07:20.630
He must have truly loved his wife.

07:21.090 --> 07:22.340
As did I.

07:22.930 --> 07:23.550
What?

07:24.050 --> 07:28.560
To be honest, I had fallen in love with Sato-dono.

07:29.730 --> 07:32.640
Of course, it was a one-sided love.

07:32.650 --> 07:35.730
With Sasayama as my rival, there was no way I could win.

07:35.730 --> 07:38.360
He truly is a nice person.

07:39.320 --> 07:41.150
And for that to happen to him...

07:48.740 --> 07:50.450
Sato!

07:53.960 --> 08:01.090
[Note: A famous Shinto legend similar to the myth of Orpheus and Eurydice.]

07:53.960 --> 07:56.710
The god Izanagi no Mikoto is said to have fled

07:56.710 --> 08:01.090
from the land of the dead in terror when he
saw the corpse of his wife, Izanami no Mikoto.

08:01.260 --> 08:06.010
But Sasayama never even
attempted to leave Sato-dono's side.

08:07.680 --> 08:13.520
These crimes continued, and there was always
a single picture on top of each discovered body.

08:14.230 --> 08:17.520
Not to mention that the pictures followed the progression
of decay depicted in the ''Nine Faces of Death" scroll.

08:19.730 --> 08:23.150
[Note: A noblewoman who was renown for her
beauty and poetry during the Heian period.]

08:19.730 --> 08:20.940
Ono no Komachi...

08:22.320 --> 08:23.150
What?

08:23.150 --> 08:27.490
No, I just remembered that something
identical to the "Nine Faces of Death" scroll exists.

08:27.780 --> 08:32.450
It apparently depicts the death of
Ono no Komachi after she came to ruin.

08:33.540 --> 08:35.080
Ono no Komachi?

08:35.080 --> 08:36.120
I see.

08:36.130 --> 08:38.960
So it is Komachi's ghost,
who is jealous of beautiful women...

08:39.130 --> 08:41.380
Umm... I was just...

08:50.140 --> 08:51.970
This is Katabira Street.

09:09.910 --> 09:13.370
Sensei, is that Ono no Komachi?

09:14.370 --> 09:15.160
Mataichi-san!

09:27.800 --> 09:29.930
Damn you, accursed mononoke!

09:30.220 --> 09:31.220
Take that!

09:48.780 --> 09:49.610
Ogin-san!

09:53.700 --> 09:56.790
Who is it that speaks my name?

10:08.220 --> 10:08.930
Ogin-san, is she okay?

10:11.800 --> 10:15.180
Sensei, you must not get further involved with Ogin.

10:32.320 --> 10:34.780
My emotions will never fade.

10:35.410 --> 10:36.450
Never...

10:48.350 --> 10:49.850
A vengeful spirit? Impossible...

10:50.640 --> 10:53.520
Sasayama, I saw it with my own eyes!

10:54.600 --> 10:57.820
While I have trouble believing it even now,

10:57.820 --> 11:00.860
it wasn't just me. Momosuke-dono saw it too.

11:02.030 --> 11:05.860
The vengeful spirit vanished, taking the
body of Momosuke-dono's friend with her,

11:06.320 --> 11:09.370
leaving behind the words,
"Who is it that speaks my name?"

11:17.920 --> 11:20.250
Ogin-san!

11:21.010 --> 11:22.210
Sensei,

11:22.550 --> 11:24.470
you must not get further involved with Ogin.

11:32.480 --> 11:35.940
Ogin died about a week ago.

11:36.730 --> 11:40.690
She went alone in order to exterminate the vengeful spirit.

11:41.230 --> 11:43.190
But instead, she herself was possessed and killed.

11:46.110 --> 11:47.030
Sensei,

11:47.660 --> 11:50.160
give up on Ogin.

11:56.000 --> 11:56.960
Ogin-san!

12:00.880 --> 12:03.460
Will you still like me, even though I'm like this?

12:09.680 --> 12:13.560
You were a denizen of a different
world from Ogin in the first place.

12:14.270 --> 12:18.770
See, you really shouldn't be involved with us.

12:19.310 --> 12:20.650
But...

12:20.650 --> 12:25.030
No matter where or how I
meet my end, you must forget me.

12:25.700 --> 12:27.030
Do you understand?

12:29.740 --> 12:32.240
Truly, I am in a grey area...

12:33.080 --> 12:35.200
I can neither live desiring the real world,

12:35.460 --> 12:38.120
nor become completely a person of the other world.

12:41.460 --> 12:45.920
Momosuke-han, a special courier
message from Edo has just come in for you.

12:45.920 --> 12:47.260
For me?

12:47.380 --> 12:52.640
It seems to be a message sent via
Tsutaya-san from your brother in Hachiouji.

12:52.810 --> 12:53.970
From my brother?

12:54.770 --> 12:58.690
Momosuke-han, your family is of samurai lineage?

12:58.690 --> 13:04.230
Yes, but I became an adapted child of the Ikomaya
family back when I was too young to remember it.

13:04.230 --> 13:06.440
So, what does your brother say?

13:06.860 --> 13:09.990
There is a matter he wishes to discuss with me.

13:09.990 --> 13:12.370
Oh, then youre going back to Edo now?

13:24.840 --> 13:28.050
It's not even as if I can meet Mataichi-san, but...

13:39.520 --> 13:41.190
Is that Sasayama-sama?

13:47.400 --> 13:48.360
Sato,

13:49.070 --> 13:50.950
why did you leave me behind?

13:51.620 --> 13:52.410
Sato...

14:28.490 --> 14:29.690
Huh?

14:33.240 --> 14:34.700
Yo, sensei...

14:35.330 --> 14:37.160
Na-Nagamimi-san!

14:37.160 --> 14:38.990
What are you doing in a place like this?

14:39.000 --> 14:40.450
Just some minor matters...

14:40.460 --> 14:43.370
I was asked by that stupid komatakuguri.

14:43.380 --> 14:46.540
Sorry to ask you this, sensei,
but would you help me carry one of these?

14:48.130 --> 14:49.920
Wh-What is this?

14:56.010 --> 14:57.640
Sorry I'm late, Sato.

15:07.440 --> 15:08.940
Sato, Sato!

15:12.700 --> 15:14.860
How much farther do I have to carry this?

15:14.860 --> 15:16.660
We're almost there.

15:16.660 --> 15:19.700
Isn't it by chance Katabira Street that lies ahead?

15:20.700 --> 15:23.460
Well then, let me take that off of your hands...

15:25.500 --> 15:26.790
Oh yes, sensei,

15:26.790 --> 15:29.840
would you hide behind that thicket over there?

15:29.840 --> 15:31.800
Just what's about to happen?

15:31.800 --> 15:33.670
Eh, watch, and you'll see.

15:37.300 --> 15:38.100
That's...

15:38.600 --> 15:40.310
What a troublesome man.

15:40.310 --> 15:42.100
It's not time for him to act yet.

15:43.600 --> 15:44.850
Nagamimi-san!

15:49.610 --> 15:50.520
That's...

15:51.690 --> 15:53.190
Hey, you there.

15:53.990 --> 15:56.160
What's inside that pack?

15:56.700 --> 15:57.950
All right, open it.

16:02.540 --> 16:03.500
Damn you!

16:05.080 --> 16:06.120
Wait!

16:22.970 --> 16:25.560
Sato!

16:27.440 --> 16:30.650
Sato, you were here? I've been looking for you!

16:31.860 --> 16:35.820
Are you the one who commits sins in my name?

16:43.500 --> 16:45.700
How brutal of you.

16:46.210 --> 16:47.080
What did you say?

16:47.670 --> 16:51.790
Your wife is no longer in this world, and yet...

16:52.800 --> 16:55.050
Are you the one who carried Sato here?

16:55.590 --> 16:59.840
You seem to be hallucinating. Look again.

16:59.840 --> 17:00.890
Ogin-san!

17:05.640 --> 17:06.930
you're alive?

17:06.940 --> 17:09.310
Or, have you wandered out as a ghost?

17:09.980 --> 17:12.400
No, that doesn't matter.

17:12.400 --> 17:14.320
I just wanted to see you again...

17:15.820 --> 17:18.280
Even if you've completely changed...

17:18.530 --> 17:20.740
I... I...

17:20.740 --> 17:23.830
And what's his point?

17:26.610 --> 17:28.000
Are you with her?

17:29.000 --> 17:30.080
Please, calm down!

17:34.300 --> 17:37.010
If you insist on maintaining your own
Way, then you will aggravate people.

17:37.170 --> 17:39.880
But if you stray from your ethics,
then you will fall into depravity.

17:41.510 --> 17:44.140
In the end, this world is naught but a dream.

17:44.510 --> 17:50.560
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

17:53.770 --> 17:55.860
Look carefully.

17:56.030 --> 17:58.190
That is not Sato-sama.

17:58.570 --> 17:59.190
What?

18:01.620 --> 18:05.030
That's a geisha from Shimabara, Kohagi.

18:05.240 --> 18:08.540
The one you killed half a year ago.

18:09.410 --> 18:11.120
There are others, yes?

18:11.370 --> 18:13.290
The young geisha Shizuno
from the entertainment district...

18:13.290 --> 18:15.920
The restaurant server Otoku, the flower-seller Okin...

18:17.550 --> 18:18.800
Impossible!

18:18.800 --> 18:22.640
All of them looked like Sato-sama to you, didn't they?

18:22.640 --> 18:24.510
My feelings for her haven't changed.

18:24.800 --> 18:28.060
Even if her body has rotted into ugliness...!

18:28.060 --> 18:31.640
Do you mean to say that is why you
copied down the progression of the bodies' decay?

18:32.150 --> 18:33.230
Like this!

18:36.360 --> 18:38.860
Your wife and the women
you killed are not happy with you.

18:38.860 --> 18:40.150
What are you saying?

18:40.900 --> 18:43.160
Even though I continue to feel
so much for them after their deaths...

18:43.160 --> 18:45.160
What would they have to be angry about?

18:45.740 --> 18:48.700
Not only did you see them in the
state they least wanted to be seen,

18:48.700 --> 18:50.000
you painted pictures of them!

18:50.620 --> 18:54.670
That's something that would even
anger the goddess, Izanami no Mikoto.

19:06.260 --> 19:07.970
You have shamed me...

19:28.870 --> 19:31.200
The deed is done.

19:34.870 --> 19:36.710
I have nothing to be ashamed of.

19:37.540 --> 19:41.260
I'll show you my emotions, my truth!

19:43.510 --> 19:46.970
By becoming a corpse just like Sato!

20:06.410 --> 20:10.280
Well, well... I guess that the nine
phases of death have been assembled with this.

20:10.740 --> 20:11.950
Ogin-san!

20:12.120 --> 20:13.870
So you were alive after all!

20:13.870 --> 20:14.910
I'm so glad!

20:15.040 --> 20:18.290
Didn't you just say you didn't care which?

20:19.210 --> 20:22.050
No, that wasn't what I meant.

20:23.880 --> 20:24.970
Nagamimi-san!

20:24.970 --> 20:30.260
Supplying you with fresh
corpses was hard work, komatakaguri.

20:30.890 --> 20:34.350
Then... What I was carrying until a little while ago was...

20:34.520 --> 20:39.770
He died a splendid death by striking
down the villain who had stolen his wife's corpse.

20:40.400 --> 20:41.690
I get it...

20:41.820 --> 20:43.820
As for what happened at his wife's funeral,

20:43.820 --> 20:47.360
he had already stolen the corpse
from the casket in advance, right?

20:47.360 --> 20:50.490
Then as the body rotted, he came to his senses,

20:50.490 --> 20:52.410
and discarded the body because he became afraid.

20:52.410 --> 20:56.790
But sooner or later his feelings
would return and he would repeat his crime.

20:58.630 --> 21:01.750
To have such emotion for his dead wife...

21:02.050 --> 21:03.250
You have it all wrong.

21:03.670 --> 21:05.760
You see, sensei,

21:05.760 --> 21:08.090
while this man was gazing at his wife's corpse,

21:08.090 --> 21:09.800
he developed a desire for her.

21:10.850 --> 21:14.180
He then lost interest in living women.

21:14.180 --> 21:18.060
That's why he killed women and indulged in ecstasy

21:18.060 --> 21:20.480
as he observed their bodies decay.

21:20.480 --> 21:21.770
How terrible...

21:21.770 --> 21:25.480
It's time for the demons to go back into the dark.

21:28.450 --> 21:31.070
Sensei, what are you going to do?

21:31.280 --> 21:33.200
Will you disappear into the darkness with us?

21:33.410 --> 21:35.660
Or, will you stay in that world?

21:38.120 --> 21:39.460
This is...

21:40.830 --> 21:43.710
Sasayama, did you slay the criminal?

21:43.710 --> 21:45.800
You did well... You did well...

21:49.510 --> 21:51.890
Ogata-sama does not know the truth...

21:52.470 --> 21:54.220
Was this for the best?

21:54.890 --> 21:57.930
In the end, this world is full of lies, sensei.

21:58.890 --> 22:02.150
Binding truth with lies and obscuring it...

22:02.690 --> 22:05.940
Isn't that how everybody lives, one way or the other?

22:06.570 --> 22:09.110
Myself and you as well.

22:09.860 --> 22:11.320
Mataichi-san...

22:14.490 --> 22:20.580
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:21.930 --> 22:28.020
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:29.000 --> 22:34.770
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:34.810 --> 22:41.440
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:42.810 --> 22:48.750
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:48.790 --> 22:55.450
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:56.290 --> 23:05.760
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:07.070 --> 23:10.270
Draw near

23:10.540 --> 23:17.540
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:17.580 --> 23:23.520
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:25.690 --> 23:30.960
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:31.000 --> 23:39.630
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:48.530 --> 23:53.790
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:55.040 --> 23:58.210
A mysterious incident torments Momosuke's older brother.

23:58.620 --> 24:02.130
A bullet of hatred penetrates the body of a samurai.

24:02.540 --> 24:05.210
The weapon is Nodeppou, hidden in the darkness.

24:06.550 --> 24:10.800
On the next Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 Stories,

24:11.260 --> 24:12.330
Nodeppou

24:12.970 --> 24:15.430
The deed is done.
